","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the range must be valid indices of the collection.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"r"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The range expression is converted to a concrete subrange relative to this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection. For example, using a "},{"code":"PartialRangeFrom","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" range expression","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"with an array accesses the subrange from the start of the range"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expression until the end of the array.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let streets = [\"Adams\", \"Bryant\", \"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]","let streetsSlice = streets[2...]","print(streetsSlice)","\/\/ [\"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The accessed slice uses the same indices for the same elements as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"original collection uses. This example searches ","type":"text"},{"code":"streetsSlice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the strings in the slice, and then uses that index in the original","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let index = streetsSlice.firstIndex(of: \"Evarts\")    \/\/ 4","print(streets[index!])","\/\/ \"Evarts\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Always use the slice’s "},{"code":"startIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property instead of assuming that its"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"indices start at a particular value. Attempting to access an element by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text